# A login nobody can use, so the staging site's basic_auth block is never empty and a Caddy
# reload never fails when the staging password is unset: every request is then 401.
# The password this hash was made from was random and thrown away. The real login is
# 10-staging.caddy beside it, made by the deploy from the STAGING_AI_PASSWORD repo secret
# (a bcrypt hash, never the password) and not kept in git (.gitignore).
# Both hashes are bcrypt cost 10 (about 60 ms), not Caddy's default 14 (about a second): anyone
# on the internet can send credentials, and each guess costs this shared box one hash.
# The secrets scanner flags any bcrypt hash; this one opens nothing (its password is gone), and
# the marker must sit on the line directly above the hash.
# nosemgrep: generic.secrets.security.detected-bcrypt-hash.detected-bcrypt-hash
locked $2a$10$SQzCB0CTKo72b.oFHhWfTuUs0b1UGTINm1zi/7X12nRqBGW0/Gu6W
